<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

<p class="date">
Effective Date: August 6, 2026
</p>

<p>
Thank you for playing <strong>Iron Ridge</strong>.
Your privacy is important to us. This Privacy Policy explains what
information may be collected when you use Iron Ridge and how it is used.
</p>

<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

<p>Depending on the features you use, Iron Ridge may collect:</p>

<ul>
<li>Device information (device model, operating system, app version)</li>
<li>Gameplay progress and saved game data</li>
<li>Achievements and leaderboard information</li>
<li>Crash reports and diagnostic information</li>
<li>Google Play Games account information if you choose to sign in</li>
</ul>

<p>
Iron Ridge does not intentionally collect sensitive personal information.
</p>

<h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>

<ul>
<li>Save your game progress</li>
<li>Provide achievements and leaderboards</li>
<li>Improve game performance</li>
<li>Fix bugs and crashes</li>
<li>Protect against fraud and abuse</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Google Play Games Services</h2>

<p>
If you sign in using Google Play Games Services, Google may collect
information according to its own Privacy Policy.
</p>

<h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>

<p>
Iron Ridge may use the following third-party services:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Google Play Games Services</li>
<li>Google Play Services</li>
<li>Google Play Store</li>
</ul>

<p>
If additional services such as analytics or advertising are added in future
updates, this Privacy Policy will be updated accordingly.
</p>

<h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>

<p>
We do not sell your personal information.
</p>

<p>Your information may be shared only:</p>

<ul>
<li>When required by law</li>
<li>To protect our legal rights</li>
<li>With trusted service providers necessary to operate the game</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Data Security</h2>

<p>
We take reasonable measures to protect your information. However,
no method of electronic storage or transmission over the Internet
is completely secure.
</p>

<h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>

<p>
Iron Ridge is not intended to knowingly collect personal information
from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information,
please contact us so we can take appropriate action.
</p>

<h2>8. Your Rights</h2>

<p>
Depending on your country or region, you may have the right to request
access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information.
</p>

<h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>

